        'photo' => 'india-5.jpg',
        'en' => [
            'headline' => 'Delhi Metro opens first Golden Line stretch linking Aerocity to Chhatarpur',
            'card_text' => 'The Delhi Metro Rail Corporation on Wednesday opened the first section of the Golden Line, a 6.2 km stretch connecting Aerocity with Chhatarpur Mandir. The section has four stations, including Mahipalpur and Vasant Kunj Sector D. Officials said it would cut travel time between south Delhi and the airport area to about 12 minutes, with trains every six minutes.',
            'key_points' => [
                'The 6.2 km stretch connects Aerocity with Chhatarpur Mandir through four stations.',
                'Trains will run every six minutes during peak hours.',
                'The rest of the corridor towards Tughlakabad is expected to open in phases next year.',
            ],
            'why_it_matters' => 'The new link gives thousands of daily commuters in south Delhi a faster, cleaner way to reach the airport area and could take some cars off busy roads.',
            'simple_text' => 'Delhi has a new Metro route. It is part of a line called the Golden Line. For now, it runs a short distance from Aerocity, near the airport, to Chhatarpur in south Delhi. There are four stations on the way. Before, people often took cars or buses through heavy traffic. Now the Metro trip will take only about 12 minutes. More stations on this line will open next year.',
            'full_text' => "The Delhi Metro Rail Corporation on Wednesday opened the first section of the Golden Line, a 6.2 km elevated and underground stretch connecting Aerocity with Chhatarpur Mandir. The section is part of the Tughlakabad to Aerocity corridor being built under Phase 4 of the Delhi Metro project.\n\nThe new stretch has four stations, including Mahipalpur, Vasant Kunj Sector D and Kishangarh, along with an interchange at Aerocity for the Airport Express Line. Officials said the journey between Chhatarpur and Aerocity, which can take 40 minutes or more by road during peak hours, would now take about 12 minutes. Trains will run every six minutes during peak hours and every eight minutes at other times.\n\nThe stations have been designed with rooftop solar panels, rainwater harvesting systems and step-free access for wheelchair users and people with heavy luggage. Feeder e-buses will connect the stations with nearby residential areas and office complexes.\n\nThe corporation said work on the remaining section of the corridor towards Tughlakabad was progressing well and was expected to open in phases next year. Once complete, the Golden Line is expected to carry over two lakh passengers a day and ease pressure on some of the busiest roads in south Delhi.",
        ],
        'hi' => [
            'headline' => 'दिल्ली मेट्रो ने खोला गोल्डन लाइन का पहला हिस्सा, एयरोसिटी से छतरपुर तक सफर',
            'card_text' => 'दिल्ली मेट्रो रेल कॉरपोरेशन ने बुधवार को गोल्डन लाइन का पहला हिस्सा खोल दिया। 6.2 किलोमीटर का यह खंड एयरोसिटी को छतरपुर मंदिर से जोड़ता है और इसमें महिपालपुर व वसंत कुंज सेक्टर डी समेत चार स्टेशन हैं। अधिकारियों के मुताबिक दक्षिण दिल्ली से एयरपोर्ट क्षेत्र का सफर अब करीब 12 मिनट में होगा।',
            'key_points' => [
                '6.2 किलोमीटर का यह खंड चार स्टेशनों से होकर एयरोसिटी को छतरपुर मंदिर से जोड़ता है।',
                'व्यस्त समय में हर छह मिनट पर ट्रेन चलेगी।',
